  (W, "The witness program is the data part of a segwit output: the bytes that follow the witness version in the output script and in the address. It is between 2 and 40 bytes long. For segwit version 0 it must be either 20 or 32 bytes, and no other length is valid; for version 1 the only length defined at the time of the book is 32 bytes, though others may be defined later [BK]."),
